1
00:00:00,721 --> 00:00:04,261
(Sheldon:)...have you ever wondered
why my little toes and lateral incisors...

2
00:00:04,433 --> 00:00:09,103
(Sheldon:)...are significantly smaller
than the average for someone of my size?

3
00:00:10,230 --> 00:00:13,940
(Leonard:)I wonder a lot of things about you,
Sheldon, but not that.

4
00:00:14,526 --> 00:00:16,156
(Sheldon:)Well, those are indicators...

5
00:00:16,319 --> 00:00:19,659
(Sheldon:)...that I'm farther along the evolutionary
scale than the average human.

6
00:00:19,823 --> 00:00:22,283
- No kidding?
- Yeah, wait, no, I'm not gonna so far...

7
00:00:22,451 --> 00:00:25,661
(Sheldon:)...as to say that I represent
a distinct new stage in humankind.

8
00:00:25,829 --> 00:00:28,459
(Sheldon:)You know, a Homo novus, if you will.

9
00:00:29,708 --> 00:00:31,788
(Sheldon:)No, that's for anthropologists to decide.

10
00:00:32,461 --> 00:00:35,751
(Sheldon:)But I am convinced
that the reason I cannot master...

11
00:00:35,922 --> 00:00:39,842
(Sheldon:)...the plebeian task of driving
is because I'm not meant to.

12
00:00:40,010 --> 00:00:42,140
(Leonard:)Yes, you are.
You're meant to learn how to drive.

13
00:00:42,304 --> 00:00:44,934
(Leonard:)- Please learn how to drive.
- No, no.

14
00:00:45,098 --> 00:00:48,848
(Sheldon:)I'm meant for greater things, like
unraveling the mysteries of the universe...

15
00:00:49,019 --> 00:00:53,819
(Sheldon:)...not determining when it's safe to pass
a stopped school bus on a country road.

16
00:00:55,609 --> 00:01:00,019
- It's never safe.
- Yeah, well, I know that now.

